    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (`AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and the full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection with 400 when an owner's email domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist.\n\n**Change in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline** \u2014 the disposable-domain check lives in the existing `ValidateOwner` step (the single step binding the request body), placed right after the syntactic email check so a syntactically valid but blocked address is rejected before being lower-cased and stored:\n\n- `ValidateOwner.java` \u2014 added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), extracts the domain after `@`, compares case-insensitively, and throws the new checked exception.\n- `OwnerEmailDisposableException.java` \u2014 new checked exception (`extends Exception`), following the repo's one-exception-per-rule pattern.\n- `OwnerEmailDisposableExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, matching the existing `OwnerEmailInvalidExceptionHandler` shape.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...OwnerEmailDisposableException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\nI used a dedicated exception rather than reusing `OwnerEmailInvalidException` because the latter's message asserts the address is *syntactically* invalid, which would be misleading for a syntactically valid disposable address \u2014 the repo consistently gives each rule its own escalation.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posts `x@mailinator.com`, expects 400) passes, and the full suite is green.",
