    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing conventions:\n\n- **Right unit.** The domain check lives in `ValidateOwner`, immediately after the syntactic email check and before the lower-case write-back \u2014 exactly where the other field validations (telephone, postcode, registration date) already live. This is email validation continuing an established block, not a new responsibility bolted onto an unrelated class.\n- **Mirrors siblings exactly.** `OwnerEmailDisposableException` matches `OwnerEmailInvalidException` (constructor message + single getter), and `OwnerEmailDisposableExceptionHandler` is byte-for-byte consistent with `OwnerEmailInvalidExceptionHandler` / `OwnerPostcodeInvalidExceptionHandler` (same `errors`/`email` body shape, same `ResponseEntity<Map<String,Object>>` 400 pattern). A maintainer would find it indistinguishable from the surrounding code.\n- **No duplication.** The blocklist is a single `Set.of` constant sitting alongside the existing `EMAIL`/`POSTCODE` pattern constants, consistently commented.\n- **Idiomatic wiring.** The escalation YAML follows the `<fully.qualified.Exception>.yml \u2192 handle: class:` convention, and the `throws` clause / javadoc were both updated coherently.\n\nNo structural improvements warranted.",
